# Third-Party Licenses

A build of this crate embeds tokenizer vocabularies published by other
parties. Since 5.1.0 the data itself ships in the tiktoken-vocab-* crates, one
per vendor, each carrying its vendor's license; this file lists all of them in
one place. The crate's own code is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT,
LICENSE-APACHE);
each vocabulary stays under its publisher's license, listed below. The full
texts are in the `licenses/` directory next to this file, and the attribution
notices the licenses require are collected in NOTICE.

Modification notice: every vocabulary was converted from its published format
(tiktoken `.tiktoken` files, Hugging Face `tokenizer.json`, Mistral
`tekken.json`) into this crate's compressed TKV1 format. Token bytes and ranks
are unchanged; for llama3, glm5 and p50k_base only the tokens beyond the
vocabulary they extend are stored.

Some licenses attach conditions to how the vocabulary, or the model it belongs
to, is used. They are quoted under each entry; read the full text before
relying on a vocabulary in a product.


